msgstr "Standard-SNMP v3-motor-id for alle nye enheder. Lad feltet stå tomt for at bruge det SNMP-motor-id, der er defineret pr. SNMPv3-notifikationsmodtager."

#: include/global_settings.php:782
msgid "Port Number"
msgstr "Portnummer"

#: include/global_settings.php:783
msgid "Default UDP Port for all new Devices.  Typically 161."
msgstr "Standard-UDP-port for alle nye enheder.  Typisk 161."

#: include/global_settings.php:791
msgid "Default SNMP timeout in milli-seconds for all new Devices."
msgstr "Standard-SNMP-timeout i millisekunder for alle nye enheder."

#: include/global_settings.php:799
msgid "Default SNMP retries for all new Devices."
msgstr "Standard-SNMP-genforsøg for alle nye enheder."

#: include/global_settings.php:806
msgid "Availability/Reachability"
msgstr "Tilgængelighed/nåbarhed"

#: include/global_settings.php:812
msgid "Default Availability/Reachability for all new Devices.  The method Cacti will use to determine if a Device is available for polling.  <br><i>NOTE: It is recommended that, at a minimum, SNMP always be selected.</i>"
msgstr "Standardtilgængelighed/-nåbarhed for alle nye enheder.  Den metode, som Cacti bruger til at afgøre, om en enhed er tilgængelig til polling.  <br><i>BEMÆRK: Det anbefales, at SNMP som minimum altid vælges.</i>"

#: include/global_settings.php:818
msgid "Ping Type"
msgstr "Ping-type"

#: include/global_settings.php:819
msgid "Default Ping type for all new Devices.</i>"
msgstr "Standard-ping-type for alle nye enheder.</i>"

#: include/global_settings.php:826
msgid "Default Ping Port for all new Devices.  With TCP, Cacti will attempt to Syn the port.  With UDP, Cacti requires either a successful connection, or a 'port not reachable' error to determine if the Device is up or not."
msgstr "Standard-ping-port for alle nye enheder.  Med TCP forsøger Cacti at sende en Syn til porten.  Med UDP kræver Cacti enten en vellykket forbindelse eller en fejl om, at porten ikke kan nås, for at afgøre, om enheden er oppe eller ej."

#: include/global_settings.php:834
msgid "Default Ping Timeout value in milli-seconds for all new Devices.  The timeout values to use for Device SNMP, ICMP, UDP and TCP pinging.  ICMP Pings will be rounded up to the nearest second.  TCP and UDP connection timeouts on Windows are controlled by the operating system, and are therefore not recommended on Windows."
msgstr "Standard-ping-timeoutværdi i millisekunder for alle nye enheder.  De timeoutværdier, der bruges til SNMP-, ICMP-, UDP- og TCP-ping af enheder.  ICMP-ping rundes op til nærmeste sekund.  TCP- og UDP-forbindelsestimeouts på Windows styres af operativsystemet og anbefales derfor ikke på Windows."

#: include/global_settings.php:842
msgid "The number of times Cacti will attempt to ping a Device before marking it as down."
msgstr "Det antal gange, Cacti forsøger at pinge en enhed, før den markeres som nede."

